{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming","id":1437562,"title":"New Werewolf 20th Anniversary edition book coming.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-01T18:07:37-08:00","id":1437562,"title":"New Werewolf 20th Anniversary edition book coming.","content":"It seems Werewolf 20 will continue for at least one more book. It's called the apocalyptic record! Check it out! <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/in-like-a-victorian-lion-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/in-like-a-vic...meeting-notes/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T22:31:39-08:00","id":1437575,"title":"","content":"My opinions gonna depend on a few things. Whose developing it? Whose writing it? And what kind of bullshit Paradox is going to try and force into it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 03-02-2021, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T00:15:29-08:00","id":1437586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1437575#post1437575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinions gonna depend on a few things. Whose developing it? Whose writing it? And what kind of bullshit Paradox is going to try and force into it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's been 3 years since Changing Ways was released.<br /> <br /> Let it go.<br /> <br /> (nvm that with all the management shake-ups at PDX and nuWW as an entity no longer being around on if the people who ordered those changes are even at the company anymore)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T00:20:32-08:00","id":1437587,"title":"","content":"I am interested in finding out what it is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T01:54:00-08:00","id":1437602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The </i><b><i>Apocalyptic Record</i></b><i> is one sourcebook containing five over-arcing stories, divided into chapters within each. These five stories tell different tales of the Apocalypse, each defined by a different phase of the moon/werewolf Auspices. Each contains a series of records, transcripts, journals, and relics written or voiced by werewolves, changing breeds, and even Wyrm-servants from </i><b><i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i></b><i>. </i><br /> This was one of those licensed <b>WW </b>IP projects that 2020 delayed discussions on, and which we\u2019re able to do now thanks to the folks at <b>Paradox</b>! As soon as they were able to give us the go-ahead after they had worked out <i>their </i>plans despite 2020, they gave the OK. And we\u2019re sooo ready to finally get our team writing! </div> </div> </div>Hm. Apocalypse was one of the best books in the whole Werewolf line, and the only End Times book that really got what the game was about. It's going to be quite an effort to have this up to scratch. I'm really curious if these are in character looks at possible apocalypses and what they mean for the people living in the pre apocalypse times, or is this going to be more of the V5/LARP after the End stuff? The first would intrigue me, the second not so much.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T15:50:41-08:00","id":1437704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1437586#post1437586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been 3 years since Changing Ways was released.<br /> <br /> Let it go.<br /> <br /> (nvm that with all the management shake-ups at PDX and nuWW as an entity no longer being around on if the people who ordered those changes are even at the company anymore)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> They need to earn that trust back. This is their chance to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 03-02-2021, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T15:52:18-08:00","id":1437705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1437704#post1437704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then drop the snark and the threadcrapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T15:55:36-08:00","id":1437707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1437705#post1437705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then drop the snark and the threadcrapping.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Neither of those things were in this thread until your post.<br /> <br /> I simply stated what information I would require in order to consider buying it.<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with a post report it to the Mods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T15:58:35-08:00","id":1437708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1437587#post1437587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am interested in finding out what it is about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the info we have I'm getting BJD vibes, which could be great, its likely to include some metaplot stuff to bring WtA in line with whatever W5 will eventually be. That has me slightly worried but as said it will depend on the writers and developer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T16:11:54-08:00","id":1437711,"title":"","content":"I, too, read the information in the block as it being a book that might be closer to &quot;Chronicles of the Black Labyrinth&quot; or &quot;The Book of Nod&quot; in style and make than an &quot;normal&quot; source book. That said, I would find it sad, if it was being the way to W5, rather than a 20th Anniversary book proper.<br /> Not that I'm particularly fond of W20, compared to 2nd and 2nd revised, but still...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T11:32:41-08:00","id":1437838,"title":"","content":"From the blurb it seems that this will be W20's version of Apocalypse, so to speak. Perhaps some scenarios will include the world continuing to exist in some form post-Apocalypse, or in the Sixth Age if you prefer. Still, if that's the case it won't necessarily be useful for groups who don't want to play The End yet.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about Apocalypse, so I don't know whether I should hope for completely new and different scenarios, or a do-over of scenarios that were disliked by players. I really, really hope it isn't &quot;SUDDENLY, AVATAR STORM!!!&quot; but worried it will be.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm disappointed just because when I saw the thread title, for a moment I had hope that the Bunyip Tribebook was un-cancelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T08:27:32-08:00","id":1438467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1437838#post1437838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the blurb it seems that this will be W20's version of Apocalypse, so to speak. Perhaps some scenarios will include the world continuing to exist in some form post-Apocalypse, or in the Sixth Age if you prefer. Still, if that's the case it won't necessarily be useful for groups who don't want to play The End yet.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about Apocalypse, so I don't know whether I should hope for completely new and different scenarios, or a do-over of scenarios that were disliked by players. I really, really hope it isn't &quot;SUDDENLY, AVATAR STORM!!!&quot; but worried it will be.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm disappointed just because when I saw the thread title, for a moment I had hope that the Bunyip Tribebook was un-cancelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's W20's version of Beckett's Jyhad Diary. Or close to it, anyway. Beckett's contained a lot of written diary entries (obviously), but as the Garou have a largely oral history, we'll have to take a different approach to format and layout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T12:43:11-08:00","id":1438490,"title":"","content":"OK thanks, but I have no idea what Beckett's Jyhad Diary is other than the adventures or discoveries of a signature character in some unknown context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T14:36:43-08:00","id":1438501,"title":"","content":"Basically trying to establish the setting and metaplot for the new edition as well as wrapping up loose ends in an 'official' capacity (though 5e might determine that). Gehenna didn't exactly occur as expected or the books suggested so what did happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T15:11:39-08:00","id":1438504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1438490#post1438490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK thanks, but I have no idea what Beckett's Jyhad Diary is other than the adventures or discoveries of a signature character in some unknown context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was basically supposed to be an IC bridge from VtM to V5 but then V5 ignored most of it anyway, its still a fun read but it references a whole bunch of signature characters and metaplot that most home games never actually featured. <br /> <br /> Matthew Dawkins, are you developing the book or are writing for it? I'll admit thats cooled me on the project a bit, I don't think our vision of the WoD is overly compatible looking at your recent output. Great quality writing just....not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:15:13-08:00","id":1439345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1438467#post1438467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, it's W20's version of Beckett's Jyhad Diary. Or close to it, anyway. Beckett's contained a lot of written diary entries (obviously), but as the Garou have a largely oral history, we'll have to take a different approach to format and layout.</div> </div> </div> </div>AT LAST, WE SHALL DISCOVER WHAT HAPPENED TO EVANS HEALS THE PAST!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I'm not even being sarcastic! I want to know!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1438504#post1438504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was basically supposed to be an IC bridge from VtM to V5 but then V5 ignored most of it anyway, its still a fun read but it references a whole bunch of signature characters and metaplot that most home games never actually featured.<br /> <br /> Matthew Dawkins, are you developing the book or are writing for it? I'll admit thats cooled me on the project a bit, I don't think our vision of the WoD is overly compatible looking at your recent output. Great quality writing just....not for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its my all time favorite vampire supplement and an amazing treat for lore buffs.<br /> <br /> I hope MD is the writer because I've never seen anyone do a deep dive on setting lore like that book did under him.<br /> <br /> I mean, we could have chapters on everything from the 7th generation to the Monkey Wrenchers to what's really going on with Samuel Haight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T01:38:00-08:00","id":1439400,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure between the tribe novels and late revised books we already know all of that.<br /> <br /> WtA was thankfully much lighter on Canon NPCs and their accompanying story lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:31:01-08:00","id":1439454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439400#post1439400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure between the tribe novels and late revised books we already know all of that.<br /> <br /> WtA was thankfully much lighter on Canon NPCs and their accompanying story lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoyed Albretch's story in the books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:40:10-08:00","id":1439455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439454#post1439454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I enjoyed Albretch's story in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wish i could articulate what makes Albretch stand out to me as &quot;this is a sample PC doing a PC's story&quot; that makes me want to keep his position open at the game table rather than use him as an NPC with all his associated events, as opposed to the Margrave who more stood out as &quot;this is a compelling NPC who provides plot hooks for PC stories&quot;. Whatever the difference is it's probably completely subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T09:01:39-08:00","id":1439461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439455#post1439455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish i could articulate what makes Albretch stand out to me as &quot;this is a sample PC doing a PC's story&quot; that makes me want to keep his position open at the game table rather than use him as an NPC with all his associated events, as opposed to the Margrave who more stood out as &quot;this is a compelling NPC who provides plot hooks for PC stories&quot;. Whatever the difference is it's probably completely subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my Own Werewolf Games:<br /> <br /> Albretch is at his most useful when he's still an exiled &quot;not quite Ronin&quot; Silver Fang who is a source of information that can provide no end of interesting insight into the structures of how Garou politics works, Silver Fangs in particular, as well as potentially adventures as well as complications. While Jacob Morningkill is alive, that provides another angle to make the PCs life difficult as they may have to protect their friend from his wrath and know WHY the Garou Nation is utterly fucked up due to having an insane 100+ year old werewolf in charge of the entirety of the New England area if not America as a whole.<br /> <br /> That Albretch is an okay NPC and one I've used many times.<br /> <br /> Albretch as KING OF THE WEREWOLVES makes things significantly less tense and you know hes going to do a good job that also makes the PCs feel less necessary. So, I always make Albretch the former rather than the latter.<br /> <br /> I think Albretch supporting a Silver Fang PC as King works better than being said king themselves. If the PCs WANT to make Albretch King versus one of their own, that's fine, but that is on them and I think Albretch would prefer they do it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T12:07:17-08:00","id":1439490,"title":"","content":"Vampire is a game whose setting has lots of secrets, and a big part of people's interest in the activities of NPCs is that we learn about those secrets. We're better understanding the Jyhad. When done right, that provides us information STs can use in the game. Unfortunately all often it just becomes a form of ersatz fiction that isn't playable. But at least it explains why people are so interested in &quot;lore&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is not a game which has many secrets. There is not some hidden Werewolf Jyhad going on. When Garou have conflicts, it's for fairly clear and obvious reasons involving issues of resources, prestige, personal animosity, and so on. Learning about NPC Garou isn't providing us information we can use in the game. In so far that the game has any secrets, its the individual plots of their enemies that the PCs have to find out and thwart.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, while Vampires are static creatures that do not age, the Garou do. We can talk about Kevin Jackson becoming Prince because Jackson and all the other vampires in Chicago By Night are essentially still the same. He's still the same Kevin Jackson we remember. The setting slightly updates, like a comic book superhero series.<br /> <br /> The Garou move on. The 16 year old kid that Evan Heals the Past was in 1992 is now 44 years old. He's unrecognizable as that small, scrawny kid. Albrecht and Mari are in their fifties - still vigorous and active as Garou, but in very different roles. An update of Rage Across New York would make it almost unrecognizable from it's 1992 origins. The Legendary Wendigo Ahroun, Cries-in-the-Wind, is probably dead. So would Mother Larissa who was Garou back in the Great Depression. And Alani Astarte. As is Accolon (although he was mentioned in Rite of Passage, not RANY) The intriguing conspiracy to seize control from the Bone Gnawers by Spotlight and Zachary Ellison? Way past resolved by now. It either succeeded or failed. The &quot;mystery&quot; behind Aeschylus, Arn Guth Stormbright, and Bladetooth also resolved. As would be the attempt of the Shadow Lords to seize the Caern of the Sentinel. Even a fair number of Garou who wouldn't be dead of old age would now be fallen in battle, or moved to different septs. You wouldn't be updating the setting so much as creating an entirely brand new one, making the occasional reference to the few NPCs still around. Unless you are someone with the skill of Alexandre Dumas, you can't pull off a Twenty Years After, Ten Years Later approach. And that's if you are treating it as fiction instead of an RPG (which you shouldn't). RANY had a very large number of hooks buried within it. Despite its flaws, an ST can do a lot with it. Any update would just erase all of these hooks, but not effectively replace them.<br /> <br /> Now I won't say there can't be interesting &quot;fan fiction&quot; done with it. It'd be interesting to read that Spotlight killed Mother Larissa, and Zachary Ellison became sept leader; or that before he died Cries-in-the-Wind lead the Wendigo, Uktena, and Red Talons taking over the Sept of the Hand of Gaia and subjugating or expelling the Children of Gaia and Black Furies there. Or that Aeschylus survived, came back and slew his father in a Challenge, and took control of the Sept of the Sentinel and successfully defeated the Shadow Lord attempt to invade that caern. That could be interesting and lead to fun hooks. But the problem is no matter what you do, it's going to conflict with other people's &quot;fan fiction&quot; - what they established in their own chronicle continuities. Or it might just not be interesting to them. It's also highly unlikely for it to be interesting because the most interesting results are probably the ones the writers could never do in published material either because it creates too much disconnect from setting expectations or for OOC reasons. There is no chance Aeschylus is ever going to be used as a character again. Wendigo and Uktena aren't going to depicted as oppressive tyrants. You're not going to show one of the iconic urban Garou, the Bone Gnawers, not be in charge of the Sept of the Green.<br /> <br /> I don't think updating the <i>Garou</i> is going to work. If such a book is going to succeed, I think it'll have to be about talking about the <i>villains</i> and other <i>concepts</i> mentioned, but never properly developed in the game. It won't be fan fiction. It'll give us something to use in games. It'll be playable.<ul><li>Show us how the Seventh Generation survived their defeat in NYC, and continues to struggle against the Garou. Ditch the ridiculous political commentary that marred it in RANY, and turn it into an interesting occult conspiracy worthy of a Delta Green sourcebook.</li> <li>Show us how Van Gelding's financial empire survived, and has mutated into some other enemy still fighting the Garou. The game needs another corporate antagonist outside of PENTEX with different aims and goals.</li> <li>Finally develop the Wagnerians and give us insight into how we can create a new kind of chronicle dealing with them. What entities did they find in their journeys that can populate a Deep Umbra chronicle, and what did they find and inadvertently bring back with them that now imperils Gaia?</li> <li>Give an interesting depiction of the Man Eaters that can be used as a significant antagonist. Show how Bonejuice lead the secret survivors of the Dandelion Hill Sept and elsewhere so that the camp survived, and regrew in strength, and how they can be used as both obvious antagonists and secret conspirators within septs. After all, if half of the Bone Gnawers are Rabble, how hard it could be not to spread there and remain secret?</li> <li>Detail one of the Fomori Families in the Appalachia, and how they created a vast network of kin and gained power so they are a significant local threat to the Garou now.</li> <li>What about the cult of Hakaken and the Shadow Lords that worship him? How do they do that? What benefits do they get? How can they hide and escape notice?</li> <li>Have the Typhon spirit succeed in its quest to free itself from Grandfather Thunder, establish a second Wyrm tribe, and one of its leading members rally the survivors of Baba Yaga's armies so there is a new and powerful Wyrm threat in Russia. Tie in the other mentions of the Typhon spirit and its fomori mentioned in Freak Legion into a single coherent faction.</li> <li>The Fianna Ossian from Kindred Most Wanted was said to be actively hunted by other Garou. He had a travelling companion, Blanca, who was a BSD disguised as a Glass Walker, and she was supposed to have a metis child with him for unknown reasons, but important to the Wyrm. Have Blanca succeed and bear that metis. What has that metis been doing? What things has he done, or could do in the future?</li> <li>Create a group of Ronin who succeed in creating some kind of community distinct from the Garou. Make it large enough so that it can't be destroyed, but make it clear there's still lots of Ronin outside of it. Make it a complex and interesting faction that isn't an outright enemy, but still a threat to the Garou by its mere existence as an alternate group for new cubs to join.</li> <li>Revisit the Gamor from Ways of the Wolf, and make them a credible antagonist faction for the game.</li> <li>It doesn't need to all be bad guys. Revisit the Valkenburg Institute and reintroduce the concept of Lunatics back into the game and how they can be an interesting part of the setting. And not just have Lunatics be humans who have not changed. Go into Lon Chaney Wolfman territory - have them go into Glabro or Lupus, but not be in control, or driven by their Beast. Give us various tools and options and how PCs can possibly help them, or permanently fail, or as a long term story device.</li> <li>Have DNA make some kind of spectacular breakthrough, and how that can change the setting while not making it gonzo. Return it to its roots of a modern hunter instead of as part of the Weaver.</li> <li>Do something interesting with the Chimera monster (not the spirit) which was in the original corebooks anf first Storyteller's Handbook, and then just dropped.</li> <li>Build some specific and interesting spirit faction for use in the Cyberrealm that would make that realm interesting to visit, or how it is expanding into the real world (or any other Near Realm; though I think the Cyberrealm has the most potential). That would add another interesting faction.</li> <li>Describe some of the monstrous banes kept imprisoned by the Bane Tenders; some that escaped and built cults and fomori around it; are examples of those banes in the Old World that were not imprisoned but would have been ones the Uktena would have done so had they been in the Old World.</li> <li>Detail one of the other Wyrm cults into a permanent and interesting faction. Build an interesting cult and story around the Pretanic Keys and Pretanic Order.</li> <li>Not seeing enough of &quot;X&quot; in the Werewolf setting, and think there should be? Create a new and interesting faction of Garou (in one tribe, multi-tribal movement) to represent that, or provide details to existing groups that could fill that role. Give them reasons to create conflicts within the Garou Nation so that it can be used to create plot. Many interesting potential factions were mentioned, but never properly developed because they were just an idea - as opposed to real characters with real organizations behind them. Too much was left to the STs to do, so these groups are actually lackluster and probably underutilized.</li> <li>Actually take the time and effort to create NPCs of the Judges of Doom camp of Shadow Lord who go around holding star chamber trials and execute &quot;criminals&quot; of the nation; and the other Garou of other tribes who oppose them. How does the Order of Our Merciful Mother work both as a camp and as part of the Catholic Church? A lot of camps are basically political factions and not true organizations, so there's not a whole lot that is needed outside of personalities. Those aren't needed in a published sourcebook unless they are driving a particular new story that has lots of potential and uses. But there are a lot of camps which are organizations and have very specific agendas, are secret conspiracies, or obviously intended as villains, and <i>these</i> are the camps that need more development - Loki's Smile, Bringers of Eternal Peace, Mechanical Awakening, Bitter Hex, Grey Raptors, Society of Bitter Frost, etc. If given more details about them, STs are more likely to use them in game, and be inspired to do more now that they have actual examples.</li> </ul>Anyone can determine the fate of King Albrecht, Mari Cabrah, Darius Winchester, Guttooth, Atahualpa &quot;Blood of the Incas&quot;, or any other canonical or signature characters. It's easy to do. Having official answers is not only lazy, it is disruptive to existing chronicles that answered those questions already are now &quot;invalidated&quot; by the new material. Going back to existing concepts that were lost in the shuffle, or never properly given bones and muscles is actually helpful, and will expand the setting. It provides <i>new</i> mysteries and challenges to be uncovered, and resurrects old ones that were forgotten or ignored for more immediate threats in the setting.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of interesting concepts, hooks, and seeds mentioned in various books, especially the early ones, and then dropped and never developed. They are unlikely to have been used by many people, and most are just forgotten. In many cases, you can even assume the PCs defeated whatever antagonist mentioned in a Rage book, but resurrect that concept somehow without invalidating the actions of the PCs. Go back to those and bring them back to the game.<br /> <br /> I am available as a consultant. My rates are reasonable. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 03-12-2021, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T14:25:08-08:00","id":1439515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439490#post1439490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is a game whose setting has lots of secrets, and a big part of people's interest in the activities of NPCs is that we learn about those secrets. We're better understanding the Jyhad. When done right, that provides us information STs can use in the game. Unfortunately all often it just becomes a form of ersatz fiction that isn't playable. But at least it explains why people are so interested in &quot;lore&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I think that actually is the appeal of Beckett's Jyhad Diary. We follow up and see what has happened to everything 20 years later.<br /> <br /> * How are the Skinwalkers tribe doing?<br /> * What happened to Evan's quest? Did he succeed or fail?<br /> * Why did the Get of Fenris murder the Swords of Heimdall? (we know the OOC reason after all)<br /> * How did the Monkeywrenchers quest against Pentex go now that hacktivism is an actual fucking thing?<br /> * Did Enron's fall in RL affect the fiction Endron oil? Was it bailed out by the government?<br /> * 20 years later, was Albretch finally killed by some Shadow Lord asshole or anti-reformist or is he still cooking?<br /> * Did the 7th Generation get wiped out or was it all on Epstein? :joke, mostly:<br /> <br /> There's a lot of lore for Werewolf to fill a book even if it's not QUITE as deep as V:TM's character driven drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T15:21:58-08:00","id":1439524,"title":"","content":"It sounds that you like RPGs to be used as literature. You want serialized stories that tell you what happens next to your favorite characters. No problem with that - I like comic books and other forms of serial fiction too - but that's not an RPG or an RPG sourcebook.<br /> <br /> I want my RPG sourcebooks to be something I can use in game, not an inferior format of presenting fiction. If I want fiction about vampires, werewolves, or what not, I already have really good options for less cost.<br /> <br /> I want toolkits that inspire me with ideas and provide me with tools I can use in game to create the kind of stories I want. I don't want to read what some other ST has decided to do with their chronicle, and then be told that is now the official version. That kind of material is what pushes me away from buying sourcebooks. Why would I care about Evan's quest if I never used that NPC in my chronicles, or what the official line about Albrecht's fate is if I already determined that in my own chronicles or if a PC in one of my chronicles became the king instead?<br /> <br /> Obviously &quot;RPGs as literature&quot; works well to boost sales as people rush out to buy to learn what happens in their game... for a while. But it drives out other players who decide they only need the books they already bought. And with each new &quot;RPG as literature&quot; book is pushed, more and more players drop out. In the medium and long term, I don't think it's a formula for success. Do you want an expanding fan base, or do you want a declining one that buys whatever you push out (for a while)? There were a lot of RPGs in the nineties who thought the latter strategy was a gold mine, and it didn't end up well for them. Maybe I'm wrong and that is a profitable path forward. But even if it is, it won't be something I'll be spending my money on. On the other hand, I think if a sourcebook came out that explore new ideas and presented new NPCs, new organizations, new details, new plots that STs can use, then that'd be something both of us would buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T15:55:29-08:00","id":1439531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439524#post1439524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds that you like RPGs to be used as literature. You want serialized stories that tell you what happens next to your favorite characters. No problem with that - I like comic books and other forms of serial fiction too - but that's not an RPG or an RPG sourcebook.<br /> <br /> I want my RPG sourcebooks to be something I can use in game, not an inferior format of presenting fiction. If I want fiction about vampires, werewolves, or what not, I already have really good options for less cost.<br /> <br /> I want toolkits that inspire me with ideas and provide me with tools I can use in game to create the kind of stories I want. I don't want to read what some other ST has decided to do with their chronicle, and then be told that is now the official version. That kind of material is what pushes me away from buying sourcebooks. Why would I care about Evan's quest if I never used that NPC in my chronicles, or what the official line about Albrecht's fate is if I already determined that in my own chronicles or if a PC in one of my chronicles became the king instead?<br /> <br /> Obviously &quot;RPGs as literature&quot; works well to boost sales as people rush out to buy to learn what happens in their game... for a while. But it drives out other players who decide they only need the books they already bought. And with each new &quot;RPG as literature&quot; book is pushed, more and more players drop out. In the medium and long term, I don't think it's a formula for success. Do you want an expanding fan base, or do you want a declining one that buys whatever you push out (for a while)? There were a lot of RPGs in the nineties who thought the latter strategy was a gold mine, and it didn't end up well for them. Maybe I'm wrong and that is a profitable path forward. But even if it is, it won't be something I'll be spending my money on. On the other hand, I think if a sourcebook came out that explore new ideas and presented new NPCs, new organizations, new details, new plots that STs can use, then that'd be something both of us would buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't think they have to be contradictory<br /> <br /> I fully admit to being a lore nerd.<br /> <br /> The books exist as entertainment and if you don't like it, don't use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:28:07-08:00","id":1439553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439515#post1439515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I think that actually is the appeal of Beckett's Jyhad Diary. We follow up and see what has happened to everything 20 years later.<br /> <br /> * How are the Skinwalkers tribe doing? <b>Answered in The Skinner.</b><br /> * What happened to Evan's quest? Did he succeed or fail? <b>Answered in the Tribe Novels.</b><br /> * Why did the Get of Fenris murder the Swords of Heimdall? (we know the OOC reason after all) <b>Answered in 2nd Ed.</b><br /> * How did the Monkeywrenchers quest against Pentex go now that hacktivism is an actual fucking thing?<b> Answered in every book published since Monkeywrenchers.</b><br /> * Did Enron's fall in RL affect the fiction Endron oil? Was it bailed out by the government? <b>Answered in BotW20.</b><br /> * 20 years later, was Albretch finally killed by some Shadow Lord asshole or anti-reformist or is he still cooking? <b>Up to the individual Storyteller.</b><br /> * Did the 7th Generation get wiped out or was it all on Epstein? :joke, mostly: <b>Answered in 2nd and again in Revised.</b><br /> <br /> There's a lot of lore for Werewolf to fill a book even if it's not QUITE as deep as V:TM's character driven drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda struggling for anything that needs answering, most of WtAs 'metaplot' was just storythooks for individual Storytellers to decide on for themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:31:48-08:00","id":1439557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439553#post1439553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm kinda struggling for anything that needs answering, most of WtAs 'metaplot' was just storythooks for individual Storytellers to decide on for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, you just gave me a major reason to want to buy it. Assembling it into one book sounds like an awesome idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:34:10-08:00","id":1439558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439557#post1439557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, you just gave me a major reason to want to buy it. Assembling it into one book sounds like an awesome idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Theres a wiki for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:37:38-08:00","id":1439560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439558#post1439558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres a wiki for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem really against this for some reason.<br /> <br /> Gathering all the metaplot in one place is fantastic and what BJD did. Things like the Week of Nightmares, Assamite defection, Invasion of the American South, LA by Night, and so on.<br /> <br /> All the stuff that other books talked about but readers might have forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T22:09:00-08:00","id":1439596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439560#post1439560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem really against this for some reason.<br /> <br /> Gathering all the metaplot in one place is fantastic and what BJD did. Things like the Week of Nightmares, Assamite defection, Invasion of the American South, LA by Night, and so on.<br /> <br /> All the stuff that other books talked about but readers might have forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its' just that as likely the last WtA book that we're ever going to get I think it would be a shame for it to be composed of reprints of already existing material and NPCs and Metaplot that only a tiny fraction of the fanbase cares about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T05:54:12-08:00","id":1439633,"title":"","content":"A lot of the old things happened for better or for worse and were left open for the storytellers and players to jump in and do something, and someone somewhere will be quite disappointed to learn their favourite plothook was resolved completely differently in a metaplot book. We learned more about the &quot;metaplot&quot; of Werewolf in novels and because some crossover book said so, than it actually advanced through most of 2nd ed and Revised.<br /> <br /> I don't think we need to know more about the signature characters and the plots of the books, we've had that already. I like Black Foxes deep dive into old plothooks a lot more, but I'm not sure we need that 20 or 30 years later. We can take a look at some of those things, but what I feel we really need is something like Delta Green's the Labyrinth. A book that takes a look into current situations, issues and all sorts of weirdness that we can make our own. The world of 1992 is not the world of 2022.<ul><li>What kind of new companies are part of Pentexes portofolio?</li> <li>What new fomori breeeds have spawned into the world?</li> <li>How about the recovery of the wolf populations in Europe, or the unified front that European Garou are showing now?</li> <li>How did Brexit impact that and are there spiritual consequences to it?</li> <li>Has the delirium evolved to help hide the shifters from the world where everyone is streaming everything or has a great deal been made with the spirits of technology to make the Veil easier to uphold?</li> <li>What kind of new movements have risen among the Garou? Good or bad ones?</li> <li>What strange new Black Spiral creeds have risen and how they terrify even the old guard?</li> <li>What's going on outside Europe and North America?</li> <li>How is the Ahadi doing? How are they impacted by the political landscape and the conservation efforts that have evolved into actual firefights with the poachers?</li> <li>The Muslim Spring ended up making things even worse in some places than others, and the writeup in Rage Accross the World (20) has aged rather poorly</li> <li>What's going on with the Stargazers and the Hengeyokai?</li> <li>What are the shifters of India like? Technically they are also a a part of the Beast courts, but I expect their courts to be different in tone, culture and style</li> <li>What's the situation like in South America? Gogol is probably gone now, and the great crusade is either over or it has changed into something different</li> <li>Rage Accross Australia was... bad. A new look at the land down under might be quite thrilling</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Fundamentally, a place that gathers dangers and hopes and where we can easily mix and match this with the old material, no matter where we took it in Our games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T07:52:33-08:00","id":1439653,"title":"","content":"The primary goal from this book is utility. If a Storyteller can't find a way of using its content to start or strengthen their chronicles, we've not done our jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:03:52-08:00","id":1439656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439653#post1439653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary goal from this book is utility. If a Storyteller can't find a way of using its content to start or strengthen their chronicles, we've not done our jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's a commendable goal, I'll keep my eye out on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:09:10-08:00","id":1439658,"title":"","content":"Which versions of BSDs/White Howlers are going to be used? W20 basically retconned the whole dynamic entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T12:00:58-08:00","id":1439697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1437562-new-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-book-coming?p=1439633#post1439633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I like Black Foxes deep dive into old plothoo